  "body": "[This](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=668172) Blink bug deals with the tests having diverged from upstream; some of this is deliberate divergence from the spec and AFAIK there are no issues here for that.\r\n\r\nSome issues:\r\n\r\n * `viewTarget` attribute normalisation is gone. (It's [dropped](https://github.com/w3c/svgwg/commit/c1690ae1b99aa95c648a304ec7a8f7dec46d7c83) from SVG 2.0 and has never had its rendering implemented in any browser.)\r\n * `filterRes` attribute normalisation is gone. (It's [sorta gone](https://drafts.fxtf.org/filters/#element-attrdef-filter-filterres) from the spec and dropped from Gecko as well as Blink (though maybe only at the parser level from Blink?).\r\n * A bunch of SVG fonts stuff is gone (again, attribute normalisation).\r\n\r\nI don't know how much else is intention deviations from the spec as opposed to being out of date with the spec.",
